  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Great Apes Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this proposal is to strengthen defenses against poaching and habitat encroachment for globally significant gibbon populations in the Nam Kading NPA by increasing enforcement staffing and expanding the coverage of patrols and investigations, and implementing a new improved system for law enforcement monitoring. Specifically, this will be done by: 1) increasing the number of staff at three checkpoints from three to six; 2) upgrading the Tad Vang Fong checkpoint to meet increasing threats due to activity related to NT1 feasibility works; 3) providing motorcycles to allow mobility to field teams to quickly respond to emerging situations that require immediate attention; 4) recruiting 6 skilled and highly motivated staff to a mobile rapid response team and ensuring that a vehicle is available for use by the mobile team at all times; 5) training of project staff in use of SMART software; 6) designing a site-specific data model; and 7) implementing the SMART system of law enforcement monitoring.</narrative>
  </description>
